    "narrative": "The primary engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today centers on **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), who anchor our production. **James Wood** is our must-start highlight, benefiting from an exploitable matchup against Chandler and a high-frequency base-stealing environment where the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his efficiency. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** projects as an elite play due to a double-barrel advantage: he faces Mahle in a park that inflates offensive output, while his platoon edge (+14%) remains the highest individual situational bonus on the roster. **Brice Turang** (75.06) rounds out the top tier, leveraging a prime lead-off spot against Rodriguez and a massive 19% SP skill boost, making him a critical component for accumulating counting stats in a favorable matchup.\n\nStrategic platoon and park adjustments have pushed several mid-tier players into viable territory, most notably **Corbin Carroll** (72.02). Despite an \"Elite Hold\" warning\u2014where the pitcher\u2019s ability to prevent stolen bases slightly drags down his upside\u2014his favorable position in the three-hole and dynamic platoon advantage make him a mandatory start. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the cut at 50.71. While **Travis Bazzana** offers high-upside potential at the top of the order, he was sidelined in favor of the defensive and platoon-stabilized efficiency provided by **Alex Freeland** and **Max Muncy**. We are keeping a close eye on the weather and potential late-scratches, though the projected matchups against high xERA starters like Sears and Rodriguez provide a solid buffer for our aggressive offensive approach today.",
